/**
 * app.js — acme-rules Dynamic Rule Engine
 *
 * POST /check
 *   Body: { "rule": "<expression>", "context": { ...fields } }
 *   Returns: { "result": true|false }
 *
 * Security note
 * -------------
 * The reference implementation in docs/RULES_ENGINE.md suggests:
 *
 *   return Function('ctx', 'req', `return (${expr});`)(ctx.ctx, req);
 *
 * This is a Remote Code Execution (RCE) vulnerability.  new Function() (and
 * eval) compile and execute an arbitrary string inside the live Node.js
 * process — an attacker can call process.exit(), require('child_process'),
 * read environment variables, exhaust memory, etc.  That pattern has NOT
 * been used here.
 *
 * Instead, rule expressions are evaluated by a purpose-built recursive-
 * descent parser + evaluator that:
 *   • never calls eval() or Function()
 *   • only allows a strict whitelist of AST node types
 *   • only resolves identifiers against the caller-supplied context object
 *   • rejects any attempt to access arbitrary global state
